WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.180
Town and country surf designs.

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:03.960
What in water rage?

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:08.080
Okay dudes, the time has come to really get radical.

00:00:08.460 --> 00:00:17.880
You and the rest of DABOYS, TNC's famous group of skate and surf crazies can kick out and pull off some awesome maneuvers together.

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:40.560
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:41.800
I'm Mike.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:43.620
I'm Joe. And I'm Sean.

00:00:44.060 --> 00:00:45.100
And I'm Sam.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:49.380
Sean, you seem to get a little radical in this episode.

00:00:49.640 --> 00:00:50.940
I'm so cowabunga, bro.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:52.820
Yeah, that is tubular, my man.

00:00:52.940 --> 00:00:53.760
My man.

00:00:53.920 --> 00:00:54.800
Wow, this is your element.

00:00:55.920 --> 00:00:57.120
Sean lived on a beach.

00:00:57.520 --> 00:00:59.900
He was abandoned by his first family and...

00:00:59.900 --> 00:01:01.220
Beaches of Lake Erie.

00:01:01.580 --> 00:01:03.300
Yeah, the beaches of Lake Erie.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.080
I wondered about that actually since you guys are, most of you are from Buffalo.

00:01:08.180 --> 00:01:09.220
Most of us, yes.

00:01:09.220 --> 00:01:10.660
You don't have beaches, right?

00:01:11.500 --> 00:01:12.620
There are beaches, yeah.

00:01:12.900 --> 00:01:14.240
There are beaches. They're not like...

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:17.820
Oh, he's committing. You know, oceanic beaches.

00:01:18.080 --> 00:01:24.140
Yeah, so nothing like, I guess, like Long Island has or, you know, as you go like along the rest of the East Coast.

00:01:24.140 --> 00:01:25.980
I mean, they're definitely beaches.

00:01:25.980 --> 00:01:29.100
They're just not very wavy beaches.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.080
I guess I just thought of them more like bays or lakes.

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:35.980
I mean, the lakes are too big for them to be like any kind of regular lake.

00:01:36.120 --> 00:01:37.340
But there's sand and stuff.

00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:40.880
There's sand. Yeah, and even like Lake Erie can have some, like, some...

00:01:40.880 --> 00:01:42.000
Not like, you're not going to surf.

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:43.320
Yeah, I'm not going to surf on them.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:44.260
It's going to be wavy, you know.

00:01:44.360 --> 00:01:51.020
Well, Joe, I'm glad you're talking about surfing because today we're talking about Town & Country Surf Designs, a game where you...

00:01:51.020 --> 00:01:53.100
Wood and Water Rage. Yeah, Wood and Water Rage.

00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:54.460
You have to say the full name. I'm sorry.

00:01:55.220 --> 00:01:56.620
Legally, you must say the full name.

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:03.160
In fact, actually, that's a point of debate because Town & Country Wood and Water Rage is what this game is often abbreviated to.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.180
People don't care for the surf designs part.

00:02:05.180 --> 00:02:12.940
The reason we mention it is because that's the actual name of the company that basically paid LJN to make this game.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:16.620
They were like, hey, video games are hot and we're a company.

00:02:16.620 --> 00:02:22.740
Company. A company. Make us a video game that naturally would fit the theme of skateboarding and surfing.

00:02:22.740 --> 00:02:26.920
So, first off, do you guys know anything about Town & Country Surf Designs?

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:27.880
I have never heard of them.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.180
No. Me neither. Okay.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.120
I really don't know anything about them at all.

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:37.720
And I think it's weird that this is our first, like, branded company NES game.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.620
You know? Wouldn't you think a McDonald's game would come out first or something?

00:02:41.620 --> 00:02:47.580
Yeah, that's what I first thought was, like, this is like those Burger King games from the mid-2000s.

00:02:47.580 --> 00:02:50.320
Yeah, I was thinking that. Like King Sneak or whatever it was.

00:02:50.620 --> 00:02:52.400
Sneak King. You know?

00:02:52.560 --> 00:02:53.540
Like, the easier one.

00:02:53.980 --> 00:02:55.200
The one that sounds like something.

00:02:55.660 --> 00:02:56.980
King Sneak would be a good game.

00:02:56.980 --> 00:02:57.960
Oh, it sounds like Sneaking.

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.100
Yeah. There were three of those Burger King games.

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:02.300
Never got any of them.

00:03:02.460 --> 00:03:06.740
They, uh, they, well, there's a guy who's collecting, like, every copy of Sneak King.

00:03:06.940 --> 00:03:10.480
And I know I've made this joke before, but no, no, that was the Shaq Fu guy.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.820
So, um, I make this connection all the time.

00:03:12.920 --> 00:03:20.580
I just think it's interesting that there are people out there devoting their Saturdays and Sundays to garage sale hunting to find copies of these games.

00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:23.620
And they're, like, and they're capital investment.

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:26.180
Like, they're actually spending all this money on them, too.

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:27.980
Yeah, but it's not getting returned to the government.

00:03:28.160 --> 00:03:39.120
So that's bad. Anyway, uh, just the only thing I could figure out was when I was looking up town and country surf designs is that these duh boys.

00:03:39.120 --> 00:03:45.420
The boys. That we keep hearing them out, and they're in the game, and they're referred to as duh boys, whether it's the manual.

00:03:45.880 --> 00:03:48.620
Yeah, they sound pretty chill. Yeah, they're the company's mascots.

00:03:49.220 --> 00:03:50.320
All of them. Not just one.

00:03:50.400 --> 00:03:53.020
All of them. I thought there were two of them that were.

00:03:53.160 --> 00:03:54.900
No, there's four. There's Cool Joe.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:56.760
Interesting. Thrilla Gorilla.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:03:59.000
Two others that I don't remember.

00:03:59.820 --> 00:04:01.300
The cat that's in the tux.

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:02.440
That one's my favorite.

00:04:02.480 --> 00:04:05.400
Well, we can definitely talk about those guys when we get to the manual section.

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.740
But, like, also, isn't this just bizarre?

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:10.700
Like, a bunch of mascots you never even heard of.

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:16.160
I really thought that we wouldn't run into something like this until, like, 89, 90.

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:19.140
This is some really weird territory.

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:23.280
Yeah, the whole thing right out of the gate is, from the moment you read the title, you're like, this is weird.

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.260
Yeah. The title sounds like the beginning of a poem.

00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.000
Like, town and country surf design, wood and water rage.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.020
Yeah, that's okay. Oh, yeah.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:35.900
That should have been the manual.

00:04:36.180 --> 00:04:37.460
You should have wrote the manual.

00:04:37.560 --> 00:04:45.800
Right. Speaking of the manual, if we'll just get into that, there are some, like, super foreign words

00:04:45.800 --> 00:04:53.260
right off the bat for me in the introduction of this thing where it's like, you know, okay,

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:56.020
dudes, the time has come to really get radical.

00:04:56.340 --> 00:05:03.760
You and the rest of da boys, TNC's famous group of skate and surf crazies, can kick out

00:05:03.760 --> 00:05:09.260
and pull off some awesome maneuvers together, whether you're jamming the ramps, jumping the

00:05:09.260 --> 00:05:13.560
cracks, riding the rails, or just laying back tall.

00:05:14.360 --> 00:05:18.740
Like, it's like, I love that they lean into this, like, this must be lingo that, like,

00:05:18.780 --> 00:05:19.740
I'm not aware of.

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:21.440
Do you know anything about this?

00:05:21.520 --> 00:05:23.740
You, you like skateboarding a little bit, right, Sam?

00:05:23.900 --> 00:05:26.640
A little bit, yeah. Laying back tall is, it's just, you know.

00:05:26.660 --> 00:05:28.480
Laying back tall sounds like a surfing term, though.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:29.740
It's like hang 10.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:31.740
Is that, is that, I don't know if anyone thinks.

00:05:31.740 --> 00:05:32.700
I thought hang 10 was surfing.

00:05:32.700 --> 00:05:34.040
But do you jam to ramps?

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.040
Yeah, hang 10 is surfing. But laying back tall sounds surfing also.

00:05:36.120 --> 00:05:38.000
Well, I don't know why. They're saying that that's all skateboarding stuff.

00:05:38.020 --> 00:05:39.420
That's skateboarding? Oh, okay.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:43.840
I thought it was like, you know how, hang 10 means that you hang all 10 of your toes off

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:44.740
the surfboard. Yeah.

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.060
Yeah, from the front.

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:50.900
And then lay back tall means like, you go into a prone position.

00:05:51.640 --> 00:05:53.540
Uh. I don't think so.

00:05:53.820 --> 00:05:57.900
No. And also just to, just to add, here's some of their surf vocabulary for you.

00:05:58.300 --> 00:06:02.540
You'll be face to face with some of the most explosive swells around.

00:06:03.160 --> 00:06:10.120
Execute some low, hard bottom turns, flawless spin outs, or just skate the lip in order to

00:06:10.120 --> 00:06:11.640
rack up some serious points.

00:06:11.860 --> 00:06:13.520
Skate the lip sounds more skating then.

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:17.440
Skate the lip? That's what I thought. Yeah, but like, you can't, can you skate the lip in this?

00:06:17.640 --> 00:06:19.580
Can you skate the lip in the surf?

00:06:19.580 --> 00:06:25.520
I assume it is the lip the, the point where it, where it, where the wave breaks?

00:06:25.700 --> 00:06:27.740
Yeah. That's what you're encouraged to do.

00:06:27.960 --> 00:06:29.160
Yeah. Encourage is very difficult.

00:06:29.940 --> 00:06:32.220
I mean, can I, or can a player?

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.340
Can you like skate it?

00:06:33.460 --> 00:06:35.520
You can surf it, but can you skate?

00:06:35.640 --> 00:06:41.360
Yeah, that's tough. And just going through the, the mascot names for a second, we already covered the best one,

00:06:41.480 --> 00:06:44.260
Thrilla Gorilla. Uh, that's fantastic.

00:06:44.620 --> 00:06:47.380
He is my favorite, yeah. Uh, then we have uninspired stuff like Tiki Man.

00:06:47.640 --> 00:06:52.280
And then we have like, I don't know, like a copyright lawsuit in Joe Cool.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.740
Like, isn't that Snoopy?

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:57.120
Oh, I thought Joe Cool was like the, the camel mask guy.

00:06:57.180 --> 00:06:58.920
Yeah, I'm just gonna say, isn't that like a cigarette thing?

00:06:59.260 --> 00:07:00.660
I thought Joe Cool was Snoopy.

00:07:00.900 --> 00:07:02.120
Maybe they're all the same guy.

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:04.200
We were all wrong and Joe Cool is this guy.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.060
I thought Joe Camel is the camel.

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:14.700
Oh yeah, right.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.180
We had no town and country at all.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.400
Or serve, or...

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:22.980
Just so, just so you know, when you type in lay back tall, you get pictures of chairs.

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:28.400
Nice. And we should note that chairs are not a playable character in this game.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:31.160
Not in this one at least. Despite how that might have enhanced it.

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:32.380
Despite the demand. Maybe it's DLC.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:39.360
Alright, so who out of the three of you thinks you can give me an overview of what you do in town and country,

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:43.080
surf designs, wood and water rage?

00:07:43.080 --> 00:07:44.280
Alright, I'll take it.

00:07:45.020 --> 00:07:47.920
So, basically you have two modes and they're pretty straightforward.

00:07:48.080 --> 00:07:49.180
The first mode is skateboarding.

00:07:49.280 --> 00:07:55.980
You are just trying to get to the end of the round while racking up as much, as many points as you possibly can by jumping over obstacles, etc.

00:07:56.380 --> 00:07:57.920
Second round is surfing.

00:07:58.220 --> 00:08:03.560
And I think your initial goal in this is to just understand what the heck you're doing and how to play this game.

00:08:03.780 --> 00:08:09.240
And then it becomes clear that you're trying to rack up points by doing things by, I guess, skating the lip.

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:16.740
And surfing within the break of the wave for as long as you can, avoiding obstacles and safely getting to shore.

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:18.540
I think that's fair.

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:28.380
I would also add that in both of those there's a time limit to, like, you know, you must complete the stage in 30 seconds or I think it's 60 seconds.

00:08:28.380 --> 00:08:31.300
No time limit in surfing, but yeah, definitely in skating.

00:08:31.580 --> 00:08:33.860
There was, I thought there would have been a time limit in surfing.

00:08:33.960 --> 00:08:36.120
You just, you sort of have to survive it.

00:08:36.320 --> 00:08:39.600
Well, okay, because I thought you can surf over to the beach whenever you please.

00:08:40.020 --> 00:08:41.620
Yeah, you can finish it pretty quickly.

00:08:41.740 --> 00:08:42.780
Okay, got it.

00:08:42.860 --> 00:08:45.660
So the time limit in that one is just more like, hey, no more points.

00:08:45.860 --> 00:08:47.680
Yeah. Like, chill it with the points.

00:08:47.680 --> 00:08:48.500
Yeah. Okay.

00:08:48.820 --> 00:08:55.320
And the skateboarding one with the timer on that one, every time you complete it, you go a little further back in the level.

00:08:55.320 --> 00:09:02.780
So you're actually playing the level, it's almost like in Super Mario Brothers, you would get the, just the flagpole part at first.

00:09:02.940 --> 00:09:07.800
And then you jump to the flagpole and then it would be like, oh, here's a little more of the level that came before that.

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.300
And then you'd play the parts that you were familiar with.

00:09:09.300 --> 00:09:10.580
It's very strange. It's just very lazy.

00:09:10.840 --> 00:09:23.020
Yeah. I think a better analogy for that, actually, if that wasn't clear, is that imagine if you did a 10 meter dash and then after successfully completing that, you do a 20 meter dash, but with the other 10 meters that you already did at the end of it.

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:23.880
Yeah, you have to start back. Yeah.

00:09:23.880 --> 00:09:26.760
Right. You just start 10 meters further each time.

00:09:27.040 --> 00:09:31.140
So with that in mind, let's just, let's just jump right into it.

00:09:31.240 --> 00:09:32.860
Let's talk about this game.

00:09:33.960 --> 00:09:36.660
I love the intro to this game.

00:09:36.780 --> 00:09:40.460
Oh, yeah. That nice, like, soft wave breeze and everything.

00:09:40.680 --> 00:09:43.260
It's funny because that sound, it's just a static sound.

00:09:43.500 --> 00:09:44.320
Yeah, just white noise.

00:09:44.320 --> 00:09:46.260
All intents and purposes, like, that should annoy me.

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.600
No, it's very nice. But just because I know it's like, it's trying to be waves.

00:09:49.800 --> 00:09:50.600
It's relaxing.

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:56.260
It was nice, but the first red flag for me came up in the title screen where there's just a yin yang.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.360
Like, I was just kind of chilling there.

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:01.080
Their logo. Their logo is the yin yang.

00:10:01.080 --> 00:10:02.460
The town and country sort of designs it.

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.100
It's specifically in those colors.

00:10:04.660 --> 00:10:06.580
Black and white? Was it black and white in the game?

00:10:06.580 --> 00:10:08.760
I thought it was like orange and purple or something.

00:10:09.020 --> 00:10:12.960
Yeah, it's usually like blue and purple, I think, is their official colors.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:15.680
Yeah, and there's like a checkerboard on the purple part.

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:17.080
Yeah. Huh.

00:10:17.540 --> 00:10:21.220
Yeah. Well, they're not really selling you on their brand, I guess.

00:10:22.380 --> 00:10:23.840
The yin yang, sum out.

00:10:23.840 --> 00:10:27.240
Yeah. I'm totally against the idea of good and evil.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:35.060
Well, just seeing like a symbol just kind of floating on the main page with...

00:10:35.060 --> 00:10:37.440
That didn't seem to have anything to do with what we were about to play.

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:41.260
Yeah, that has nothing to do with anything. It just seems like kind of, you know, a red flag to me.

00:10:41.260 --> 00:10:44.480
And what's worse is like town and country surf designs are still around.

00:10:44.500 --> 00:10:49.340
So they have like not done any more brand awareness since this NES game.

00:10:49.560 --> 00:10:51.180
I think they're based in Hawaii.

00:10:51.480 --> 00:10:52.420
They're like a Ron John.

00:10:53.160 --> 00:10:54.820
Oh, okay. Yeah. Okay, fine.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.020
But in Hawaii. Right, exactly.

00:10:57.900 --> 00:11:02.160
Okay, so let's just, let's talk about the skateboarding section of this.

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:06.700
As we mentioned, you have to skate through the level and there's like obstacles along the

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.880
way that try to like knock you over.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:14.760
You're capable of jumping with your skateboard or without it.

00:11:15.140 --> 00:11:16.720
Yeah. You know, I don't know.

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:18.360
Like it seems like...

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:19.220
What's the purpose of that?

00:11:19.660 --> 00:11:25.160
I really like the like pre Tony Hawk skateboarding media.

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:29.640
Yeah. Because it has like this really weird idea of what skateboarding is.

00:11:30.020 --> 00:11:33.160
And like, it's sort of like in...

00:11:33.160 --> 00:11:39.020
I forgot what exactly there, but I think a lot of made for TV shows and movies had skating

00:11:39.020 --> 00:11:42.380
scenes where they're not really doing tricks so much as just staying upright.

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:44.320
It's a vehicle for them almost.

00:11:44.460 --> 00:11:45.440
It's like this is how we get around.

00:11:45.740 --> 00:11:48.200
And that's just what this game is doing with skateboarding.

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:49.600
You're just on your way to surf.

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:57.760
Yeah. And so like, you know, these obstacles come throughout the stage, but they, there's really like no

00:11:57.760 --> 00:12:00.000
rhyme or reason to these enemies.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.800
There's like a toy car.

00:12:02.000 --> 00:12:03.540
Yeah. A turtle.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:06.060
And you can jump on the turtle for points.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.100
Yeah. It's messed up.

00:12:07.240 --> 00:12:09.440
Yeah. I think that we're thinking about this the wrong way.

00:12:09.520 --> 00:12:12.100
They're not enemies. Like this is supposed to be a simulation.

00:12:12.160 --> 00:12:13.340
It's just obstacles.

00:12:13.540 --> 00:12:17.940
Maybe they're not like, maybe there's no cars because there's like holes all over the

00:12:17.940 --> 00:12:23.380
sidewalk too. You have like, you know, the caution barriers and you have the holes you have to jump over.

00:12:23.380 --> 00:12:27.200
And so that's why there's a difference between jumping with your skateboard and without it,

00:12:27.200 --> 00:12:31.960
because if it's a barrier, you can do this cool trick where you jump with just you and

00:12:31.960 --> 00:12:33.260
then land back on your skateboard.

00:12:33.640 --> 00:12:37.380
But if there's a hole, you'll jump without the skateboard and the skateboard will just

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.860
fall into the hole and you'll just collapse.

00:12:40.100 --> 00:12:41.840
Right. Because you can't stand up without your skateboard.

00:12:42.480 --> 00:12:45.420
Absolutely. Yeah. That was an interesting thing.

00:12:45.620 --> 00:12:49.520
I thought it was, I thought it was like, okay, it's interesting that they gave you the

00:12:49.520 --> 00:12:50.860
option to jump without your skateboard.

00:12:50.860 --> 00:12:52.960
So your skateboard can slide through while you go over something.

00:12:52.960 --> 00:12:56.280
But there's only one obstacle in the game that needs that.

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:57.520
And they just put it everywhere.

00:12:57.520 --> 00:12:58.700
So you'd have to use it a lot.

00:12:58.840 --> 00:13:00.620
And I feel like that was a little happy.

00:13:00.900 --> 00:13:02.800
You could just, yeah, you could also just jump over it too.

00:13:02.980 --> 00:13:08.240
Like I thought it was annoying also that the regular just Ollie, you know, is you have

00:13:08.240 --> 00:13:13.520
to hit back and a for it to happen at the same time, which I don't know, just make

00:13:13.520 --> 00:13:15.080
it be, you know, why not?

00:13:15.260 --> 00:13:19.660
I thought that was annoying at first too, until I started like kind of getting the feel

00:13:19.660 --> 00:13:22.780
for it. It sort of feels good to control that.

00:13:22.780 --> 00:13:27.640
Not only that, but it's the only source of challenge in this mode of the game.

00:13:27.840 --> 00:13:32.560
Yeah. In fact, you know, the graphics are pretty nice in this game overall.

